e03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "grade level", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the year an elementary or secondary student is enrolled in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  At the lower grade levels, it includes everyday skills such as writing checks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "financial literacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "understanding how money and the economy work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These workbooks are designed to help teachers explore financial literacy in the classroom.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stock market", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an institution where shares in public companies and other financial products are traded", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The workbooks explore more complicated notions such as understanding the stock market and planning for retirement.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "check", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small piece of paper a person signs to inform a bank to move money to a different account", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Students will learn how to write checks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "economy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the study or the management of financial activity in a country or a community", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In advanced mathematics courses, you could teach students about the economy or how banking works.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Intonation with Non-Final Thought Groups", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When a sentence is divided into two (or more) thought groups or clauses, each thought group has its own intonation pattern.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If the two groups are separate thoughts, you use a rising-falling pattern at the end of the first thought, and then a falling pattern at the end of the final thought.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">To tell you the <span class=\"underline\">truth</span>,// it can't be <span class=\"underline\">done</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If there is a connection between the two sentences, you use a rising intonation on the final stressed word.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If you make me,// I'll <span class=\"underline\">do </span>it.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the beginning group ends with a rising pattern, this will create a feeling of <span class=\"underline\">suspense</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If you want to get a <span class=\"underline\">promotion</span>,// you'll have to work harder.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read these examples from the text. Determine the correct intonation pattern. Listen to the dialogue to check.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "At BFP Publishing,// we know that schools are busy places. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "At the upper grades,//  the workbooks can be used in history courses to help understand the Great Depression.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " How to Deliver a Sales Pitch", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " An effective sales pitch is a cooperative effort -- a conversation where you listen to the buyer, ask real questions, and offer them a solution to a challenge they're experiencing.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "It's important to start with a great first impression. Begin with a catchy, relevant one-liner. Captivate your audience and go from there. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Make sure you research your target audience/buyer. Understanding your customer is the first step in creating a great sales pitch.</li><li>Identify what they need and show them that you've done your research. Tell them how to solve their problem or increase productivity.</li> <li>Have a referral ready. They are likely to complete a sale better than any other methods.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose any product or service you know well, like a brand of car, a certain holiday destination, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 80 - 100-word sales pitch to sell the product or service. Follow the structure of a sales pitch in this lesson.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sales pitch to a partner. Use proper intonation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask for feedback and advice on how to improve the sales pitch.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a sales pitch to sell a product or service.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read the sales pitch using correct intonation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for advice to improve the pitch.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}